    "text": "Two point charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>10</mn></msqrt><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#956;C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#956;C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> are placed on the <math><mi>x</mi></math> -axis at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> respectively. The electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>in</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> at a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> on <math><mi>y</mi></math>-axis is,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>Take</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>",
